<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!-- No engine-side hit ceiling: a query returns what it asks for.

     Vespa's own defaults (maxHits 400, maxOffset 1000) SILENTLY TRUNCATE a
     larger request, so leaving these fields out is not "no limit" — it is a
     400-hit limit. Int.MAX_VALUE is how you say "don't cap"; the only bound
     left is the caller's own `limit` (and the host's memory).

     Deciding a policy cap is the OPERATOR's call, not the library's: lower
     these if you want the engine to refuse expensive queries. Note that a
     full-corpus dump should use a document/v1 visit (VespaEventIndex.visitIds)
     rather than a huge search — it streams instead of materializing. -->
<query-profile id="default">
    <field name="maxHits">2147483647</field>
    <field name="maxOffset">2147483647</field>
</query-profile>
